From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:50:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/40] test(proofs): Counterexamples.lean after the FC-01 fix
 (reduced d116a64; the fix itself is 4a38b91)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Original subject: fix(FormatIO): print numbers with exponent < -maxExponent as exact decimals

render printed J.num m e with e < -30 as "{m}e{e}". Numbers parsed from text can
have e < -1000 (1.5e-1000 is stored as 15*10^-1001), so `figram fmt` / Api.fmt wrote
text that figram itself rejects ("показатель степени по модулю больше 1000"),
although the document passed `check` (check_roundtrip only covers the J model).
Such numbers are now printed as exact decimal fractions, which parse back to the
same (m, e).

Regression test: audit/proofs/TextRoundTrip.lean (5 of 15 cases FAIL before, all PASS
after); REPRODUCTIONS/fmt_exponent.sh. golden.jsonl and pizza.bot.json unchanged;
json_fuzz 2x30000 cases, 0 mismatches.

Integration note: FC-01 is fixed by 4a38b91 (formats-correctness), whose render
condition is the same predicate (-maxExponent <= e) and gives byte-identical output; this
commit keeps only the audit/proofs/Counterexamples.lean adjustment, the FormatIO.lean and
FORMAT.md hunks were dropped as duplicates.

(cherry picked from commit d116a649ac8efb9a867629e804c858cb7e59e07a)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JgWRtX2jyUidN8gxEhe5qx
---
 audit/proofs/Counterexamples.lean | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/audit/proofs/Counterexamples.lean b/audit/proofs/Counterexamples.lean
index a93d708..ffea5b5 100644
--- a/audit/proofs/Counterexamples.lean
+++ b/audit/proofs/Counterexamples.lean
@@ -97,10 +97,10 @@ def expText : String :=
 #guard match parse expText >>= decode with
   | .ok d => d.check.isEmpty
   | .error _ => false
--- but the canonical text written by `print (encode d)` (what `figram fmt` writes) is rejected:
-#guard match parse expText >>= decode with
-  | .ok d => (match parse (print (encode d)) with | .ok _ => false | .error _ => true)
-  | .error _ => false
+-- On baseline d69bbaf the canonical text written by `print (encode d)` (what `figram fmt`
+-- writes) is "…15e-1001" and is REJECTED by `parse` (LOGS/09-counterexamples.stdout).
+-- The fix in Figram/FormatIO.lean (`render`) makes it parse; the asserting regression test
+-- is audit/proofs/TextRoundTrip.lean. Here we only show the current behaviour:
 #eval match parse expText >>= decode with
   | .ok d => print (encode d) ++ "\n=> " ++ (match parse (print (encode d)) with
       | .ok _ => "parsed" | .error e => "parse error: " ++ e)
